# Hash-provenance demo assets (#871) must be byte-for-byte identical on every
# platform — forgeSpec.test.ts asserts each committed dashboard HTML's exact
# byte length + sha256. Windows checkout would otherwise convert LF→CRLF and
# inflate the byte count, breaking the provenance assertion. Treat as binary
# (no EOL conversion) so the working tree matches the committed bytes everywhere.
assets/forge-demo/*.html -text

# Storyboard docs (#1120) feed the approved-storyboard gate, which pins
# docSha = sha256(line-ending-normalized doc). Belt-and-suspenders: keep the
# storyboard text files LF on checkout EVERYWHERE so a Windows CRLF checkout
# can't drift the working-tree bytes (the gate already normalizes EOLs before
# hashing, so this is defense-in-depth, not the sole guard).
storyboards/** text eol=lf

# Kanban demo board snapshot JSON (#1120) — byte-stable provenance; keep LF off Windows autocrlf.
assets/kanban-demo/*.json -text

# Bundled Inter font binaries (#1156) — pure binary; never apply EOL conversion (a Windows CRLF
# checkout would corrupt the woff2 bytes). buildInterFontFaceCss reads these bytes verbatim.
assets/fonts/Inter/*.woff2 -text
# The SIL OFL license text must travel with the fonts; pin it -text so the #871 assets/ EOL guard
# (gitattributesEolPin.test.ts) is satisfied and a Windows checkout can't CRLF-mangle it.
assets/fonts/Inter/*.txt -text
